WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Today we look at binary search. The idea is to halve the search space every step, which gives logarithmic running time on a sorted array.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Next, hash tables. When two keys collide we can use chaining, where every slot holds a linked list of entries.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Finally graphs. Breadth-first search uses a queue and visits the vertices level by level; depth-first search uses a stack and backtracks.
